ndhra Pradesh State Police and \nthe steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *209 FOR \nANSWER ON 03.08.2021 ON THE SUBJECT OF “MODERNISATION OF \nPOLICE FORCE” \n \n(a) to (c): „Police‟ and „Public Order‟ are State subjects under the seventh \nSchedule of the Constitution of India.  However, the Government of India \nsupplements the efforts of the State Governments towards equip ping and \nmodernizing of their police forces, under the centrally sponsored scheme \nof „Assistance to States for Modernisation of Police‟. Under the scheme, \nupto 20% allocated funds are earmarked for providing incentives for \nimplementation of Police reforms.  Andhra Pradesh is one of the six States \nidentified for award of this incentive during 2019 -20 and an amount of \nRs.35.98 crore was released. The State Government planned to utilize this \namount for the following projects: \ni. Construction of Integrated Command & Control Centre for North \nCoastal Zone,  \n \nii. Weapon Management Project in 5 units,  \n \niii. Upgradation of Digital UHF Trunking System,  \n \niv. Palm Print Live Scanners & Mobile AFIS systems for Finger Print \nBureau of CID,  \n \nv. Procurement of Hardware of CCTNS Project  \n \nvi. Smart Policing & Training Infrastructure.   \n \n\n \n-3- \nL.S.S.Q.NO.*209 FOR 03.08.2021 \n \n(d): The funds allocated and released to Andhra Pradesh for \nmodernization of State police force under this scheme during the last \nthree years are as below: \n(Rs. in crore) \nYear  Allocation  Release Remarks  \n2018-19 26.48 50.81 Released amount include better performance \nincentives of Rs.14.81 crore & incentives for \npolice reforms of Rs.7.69 crore \n2019-20 24.46 75.36 Released amount include better performance \nincentives of Rs.14.92 crore & incentives for \npolice reforms of Rs.35.98 crore \n2020-21 24.46 5.83 Less release due to substantial unspent \nbalance with the State \n \nIn addition, the Government of India also released funds to the \nGovernment of Andhra Pradesh for setting up / upgradation of Forensic \nScience Laboratories (Rs. 42.35 crore) and for Greyhounds Training Centre \n(Rs. 9.08 crore) during the years 2017-18 and 2018-19.  \n \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |21", "t": "Promotion of Modern Farming", "head": "O.I.H.\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n21\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n \n20\nTH\n \nJULY, 2021\n \n \nPROMOTION OF MODERN FARMING\n \n \n†*21. \n   \nSHRIMATI JASKAUR MEENA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government is promoting modern farming alongwith traditional farming in \nthe country; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif\n \nso, the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government is providing facilities to promote modern farming in the \ncountry and if so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has also fixed any target to promote modern farming; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nif so, th\ne details thereof including the present achievements in this regard?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (e\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\ne\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n21\n   \nDUE FOR REPLY ON\n \n20\nth\n \nJULY, 2021\n.\n \n \n(\na) to (e):\n \nThe Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare\n \nunder various \nmissions/schemes is promoting and extending supports\n \nto the farmers for various modern \nfarming technologies to sustain growth of agriculture through infrastructure development \nsupports for establishment of Custom Hiring Centres/Hi\n-\ntech Hubs of agricultural machines. \nUnder Mission for Integrated Development o\nf Horticulture (MIDH)Scheme, for protected \ncultivation of horticulture and vegetable crops, since 2014\n-\n15 to 2020\n-\n21, an amount of \nRs.2763.35 crore have been released and an area of more than 2.33 lakh\n \nhectare has been \ncovered. Production and distribution \nof certified /quality\n \nseeds of 165.08 lakh quintal has \nbeen done against the requirement of 154.50 lakh quintal in Kharif 2021.In Kharif1933468 \nquintals of hybrid seeds were made available against the demand of 1906633 quintals.\n \nResources conservation tech\nnologies\n \nfor water use efficiency enhancement through micro \nirrigation has been promoted under Pradhan Mantri\n \nKrishi\n \nSinchayee Yojana\n \n(PMKSY). \nUnder PMKSY, funds of Rs.14548.03 Crore have been released since 2015\n-\n16 to 2020\n-\n21 \nand an area of 57.31 lakh hec\ntare was brought under micro irrigation.\n \n \nSoil Heath Cards distribution to farmers for soil test based balanced and judicious use \nof fertilizers has been undertaken and a total of 107412648 soil health cards have been \nissued during Cycle\n-\nI (2015\n-\n17) and 11\n9450316during cycle \n–\nII(2017\n-\n19).The institutional \nsupport is provided through \ntechnological interventions under Pradhan\n \nMantri\n \nFasal\n \nBima \nYojana (PMFBY). Under PMFBY as against the premium amounting to Rs.21614 crore\n \ncollected from farmers since inception of the scheme in 2016\n-\n17, so far claims amounting to \nRs.97719 crores\n  \n \nhave already \n   \nbeen\n  \n \npaid to about 834.6 lakh farmers.\n \nUnder PM\n-\nKISAN, \n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n\n \nfinancial benefits of approximately 1.37 lakh crores has bee\nn given to more than 11.08 crore \nbeneficiaries.\n \nUnder digital\n \nagriculture, precision\n \nfarming is promoted by use of drones in \npesticide spraying for locust control. The \ndissemination of all the agriculture related \ninformation to the farming community is don\ne through various delivery channels including \nSMSs, farmer’s portals, mobile apps etc. \n \n \nKeeping in view the vital role of agricultural mechanization to modernize agriculture, central \ngrants amounting to Rs. \n4865\ncroreshave been released to the States during the period from \n2014\n-\n15 to 2021\n-\n22through which more than 1323000 machines have been distributed to \nfarmers and more than15400 Custom Hiring Centres, 360 Hi\n-\ntech hubs and 14200 Farm \nMachinery Banks have been es\ntablished to make machines and equipments available to \nfarmers on rental basis. These interventions have helped in increasing the farm power per \nunit area for performing various agricultural operations by 43 % than in 2013\n-\n14.\n \n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |210", "t": "Damaged Foodgrains", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF IilDIA\nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTIOil\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.2{ O\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 3RD AUGUST, 2O2{\n*2IO. SHRI D.K. SURESH:\nSHRIMATI SUMALATHA AMBAREESH:\nWilt the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS' FOOD AND PUBLIG\nDISTRIBUTIoN Tctirfaf arri, ur<-+ 3ik Trdafu Fittur d* be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether huge quantity of foodgrains is damaged in various godowns\nof Food Gorporation of lndia (FGl);\n(b) if so, the details thereof during the last three years, State'wisel\n(c) the estimated loss incurred due to damaged foodgrains; and\n(d) whether the Government has taken steps to prevent such loss of\nfoodgrains in FGI and if so, the details in this regard?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF GOMMERGE & INDUSTRY, GONSUMERAFFAIRS, FOOD &\nPUBLIC DISTRIBUTION AND TEXTILES\n(sHRr PTYUSH GOYAL)\n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\nDAMAGED FOODGRAINS\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (d) OF THE\nSTARRED OUESTIO]{ T{O. *2{O DUE FOR ANSWER ON O3.O8.2O2{ IN THE\nLOK SABHA.\n(a): No Sir.\n(b): Does not arise in view of the (a) above.\n(c): The foodgrains procured for Gentral Pool Stocks are stored in\ncovered godowns and Gover & Plinth (GAP) storage. The foodgrains are\nstored as per prescribed procedure/guidelines of Food Gorporation of\nlndia (FGl). But a meagre quantity of foodgrains may get\ndamaged/become non-issuable during storage due to transit damage viz\nenroute damage in wagon/truck, contamination, wagon roof leakage and\nnatural calamities like cyclone/flood etc. During the year 2O2O'21 a\nguantity of {85O Tonnes foodgrains have been damaged in godowns of\nFGI which is O.OO3% of total foodgrains quantity handled and its\nestimated value is Rs. 2.57crore\n(d): Steps taken by the Government to Prevent damage of foodgrains\nare enclosed at Annexure.\n\nANNEXURE\nANNEXURE REFIERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF STARRED\nQUESTION NO. \":2IO DUE FOR ANSWER ON 03.O8.2O2{ IN LOK SABHA.\nSTEPS TAKEN BY THE GOVERI{MENT FOR SAFE STORAGE OF\nPROCURED FOOI'GRAINS TO PREVENT DAMAGE:\nA. Periodical nnaintenance of scientific storage structure.\nDedicated Engineering wing of FG! is carrying out periodical\nmaintenance of all storage structures.\na) ldentifying & repairing of al! the leakage points in the roof.\nb) Gleaning of drainages in the godown premises ensured.\nc) Ensuring that no seepage inside the godowns so that no clogging\nup of water.\nd) Ensuring all the repairing works are attended on priority before\nthe onset of monsoon season,\nB. Gapacity burilding for additional modern storage structure.\nSteel Silo bins are being constructed as a measure of modern\ncapacity building which ensures better preservation of foodgrains\nand enhances its shelf life.\nG. Scientific sttorage and preservation of stocks.\n(i) Foodgrains are stored by adopting proper scientific code of storage\npractices.\n(ii) Adequate dunnage materials such as wooden cratesr bamboo mats,\npollrthene sheets are used to check migration of moisture from the\nfloor to the foodgrains.\n(iii) Fumigation covens, nylon ropes, nets and insecticides for control of\nstored grain insect pests are provided in all the godowns.\n(iv) Prophylactic (spraying of insecticides) and curative treatments\n(fumigation) are carried out regularly and timely in godowns for the\ncontrol of stored grain insect pests.\n(v) Effective rat control measuresr both in covered godowns as well as\nin Govered and Plinth (CAP) storage are used.\n.......2t-\n\n-2-\n(vi) Regular periodic inspections of the stocks/godownsare undertaken\nby qualified and trained staff and senior officers. The health of the\nfoodgrains is monitored at regular intervats by a system of checks\nand super checks at different levels. Following Ghecks and Super\nchecks are conducted in the godowns by FGI to ensure proPer\npreservation of foodgrains in the storage.\na) Fortnightly inspection of stocks on { OOo/o basis by Technical\nAssistant.\nb) Monthly inspection by Manager(QG)\nc) Quaderly inspection by AGM(aC)\nd) Super Ghecks by Regional' Zonal and FGI Hqrs Squads.\n(vii) The principle of rFirst in First Out\" (FIFO) is followed to the extent\npossible so as to avoid longer storage of foodgrains in godowns.\nBesides stocks lying at vulnerable plinths and procured under\nrelaxed specifications are issued on overriding priority to avoid any\ndamage to stocks in storage.\n(ix) While movement PolXthene Sheets are spread on the floor of railway\nwagons to retrieve the spilled-over grains to avoid contamination to\nstocks.\n(xi) lmmediate action to segregate & recondition of the stocks\nwhenever it gets affected.\n(viii) Only covered rail wagons are used for movement of foodgrains so\nas to avoid damage during transit.\n(x) Damage Monitoring Gells have been set up at Districtr Regional and\nZonal tevels to regularly monitor quality of stocks and reduce\ndamages. Each case of damage is thoroughly investigated and\ndisciplinary action, wherever required, is invariably taken against\nthe delinquents."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |211", "t": "Increasing Agricultural Land under Irrigation", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND \n \nFARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n211\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n \n3\nrd\n \nAUGUST, 2021\n \n \nINCREASING AGRICULTURAL LAND UNDER IRRIGATION\n \n \n \n*211. \n  \nSHRI ANUBHAV MOHANTY: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether it is a fact that in order to achieve the objectives of National Food Security \nMission, the Government is planning to increase agricultural land under irrigation; and \n \n \n(b) \n \nif\n \nso, the details of proportion of increase in land under irrigation planned by the \nGovernment?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) &\n \n(\nb\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table \nof the House.\n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN \nREPLY TO PARTS (a) &\n \n(\nb\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n211\n   \nDUE FOR REPLY ON\n \n3\nrd \nAUGUST, 2021\n.\n \n \n(a):\n \n \nDepartment of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare (DA&FW) \nis implementing \nthe \nNational Food Security Mission\n \n(NFSM)\n \nin the country \nwhich aims at \nincreasing \nthe \nproduction of rice, wheat, pulses, coarse cereals (maize and barley), nutri\n-\ncereals (jowar, \nbajra, ragi and small millets)\n, \nand oilseeds and oil palm through area expansion and \nproductivity enhancement in\n \na sustainable manner in the identified districts of the country\n. \nThe objective of the mission is also for r\nestoring soil fertility and productivity at the \nindividual farm level\n, e\nnhancing farm level economy to restore confidence amongst \nfarmers\n.In order t\no encourage water use efficiency, \nassistance is being provided to the \nfarmers for purchase of pumpsets, water carrying pipes, sprinkler sets and mobile raingu\nn \nthrough the State Governments and Union Territories (\nUTs\n) under NFSM.  \n \n \n(b):\n \nGovernment is implementing Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) \nwith the objective to enhance physical access of water and expand cultivable area under \nassured irrigation, improve on\n-\nfarm water use efficiency, introduce sustainable water \nconserva\ntion practices, etc. The components of PMKSY are as under:\n \n \ni\n.\n \nAccelerated Irrigation Benefit Programme\n \n(AIBP): \nMajor and Medium Irrigation \nprojects including National projects\nare\n \nb\neing implemented by \nthe \nDepartment of \nWater Resources River Development & Gang\na Rejuvenation (DoWR, RD&GR). \nDuring 2016\n-\n17 under PMKSY\n-\nAIBP, 99 projects having ultimate potential of 76.03 \nlakh hectare have been prioritized for completion. Out of which, 41.39 lakh hectare \nof irrigation potential was created upto March, 2016. Against \nthe balance ultimate \npotential of 34.64 lakh hectare, 22.47 lakh hectare has been \nachieved till M\narch, \n2021. \n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n\n-\n2\n-\n \n \nii\n.\n \nPMKSY\n-\nHarKhetKoPani (HKKP): Source Augmentation, distribution, ground water \ndevelopment, lift irrigation, diversion of water \nfrom w\nater plenty to water scarce\n \nareas, \nrepair, restoration, renovation of traditional water bodies are being implemented by \nDoWR, RD & GR\n \nu\nnder PMKSY\n-\nHKKP\n. In Ground water irrigation component, 0.36 \nLakh ha command area has\n \nbeen covered during last two years (\n2019\n-\n21)\nand u\nnder \nSurface Minor Irrigation scheme\ns\n, \nthe target irrigation potential creation is 10.529 lakh \nhectare and out of which 6.84 lakh hectare is reported created upto March, 2021. \nUnder Repair, Renovation and Restoration (RRR)\ncomponent\n, target irrigation potential \nrestoration of these schemes is 1.89 lakh hectare and out of this, 1.319 lakh hectare is \nreported to be restored till March, 2021. \n \niii\n.\n \nPMKSY\n-\nPer Drop More Crop (PDMC): Focuses on enhancing water use efficiency at \nfarm level throu\ngh Micro Irrigation viz. Drip and Sprinkler Irrigation System being \nimplemented by DA&FW. An area of 57.3 lakh ha under micro\n-\nirrigation has been \ncovered during 2015\n-\n16 to 2020\n-\n21 under PMKSY\n-\nPDMC.\n \niv\n.\n \nPMKSY\n-\nWatershed Development Component: Ridge area treatmen\nt, drainage line \ntreatment, soil and moisture conservation, water harvesting structure, livelihood \nsupport activities and other watershed works being implemented by Department of \nLand Resources. Under PMKSY\n-\nwatershed component, 7.53 lakh water harvesting \ns\ntructures have been created /rejuvenated. An additional area of 16.07 lakh ha has \nbeen brought under protective irrigation during the period from 2014\n-\n15 to 2020\n-\n21.\n \n \n*******\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |212", "t": "Economic Status of the Village Panchayat", "head": " GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 212 \nANSWERED ON 03.08.2021 \n  \nECONOMIC STATUS OF THE VILLAGE PANCHAYAT \n  \n*212.   SHRI KALYAN BANERJEE: \n  \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has made any survey regarding the economic status of the \nvillage panchayat during the Covid-19 pandemic; and \n(b) if so, the details including outcome thereof; \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n  \n(a) & (b)  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN PARTS (a) & (b) IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 212 FOR ANSWER ON 03.08.2021 REGARDING \nECONOMIC STATUS OF THE VILLAGE PANCHAYAT \n___________________________________________________________________________ \n  \n(a)   No, Sir. \n  \n(b) In view of (a) above, does not arise. \n  \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |213", "t": "Public Service Commission in Puducherry", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*213 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 03RD AUGUST, 2021/ SRAVANA 12, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nPUBLIC SERVICE COMMISSION IN PUDUCHERRY \n \n*213.  SHRI VE. VAITHILINGAM: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that there is no separate  Public Service \nCommission in the Union Territory of Puducherry; \n \n(b) whether the Government has any proposal for  setting up of Puducherry \nPublic Service Commission for Government jobs; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n-2- \nPOSITION NO.13 \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NUMBER *213 \nFOR 03.08.2021 \n \n \n(a): There is no separate Public Service Commission in the Union \nTerritory of Puducherry as it does not come under the definition of ‘State’ \nin so far as Article 315 (1) of the Constitution of India is concerned. \n \n(b) & (c): There is no such proposal.  \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |214", "t": "Work to Labourers under MGNREGS", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.214 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.7.2021 \n \nNew Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas in Delhi NCR \n \n214. SHRI MANOJ TIWARI: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to establish new Navodaya \nVidyalayas in the country in near future including Delhi NCR especially in North East \ndistrict constituency; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (c): The Navodaya Vidyalaya Scheme envisages opening of one Jawahar \nNavodaya Vidyalaya (JNV) in each district of the country. All the districts (as on 31st \nMay, 2014) of the States/UTs, which have accepted the scheme, have been \ncovered. As on date, 661 JNVs have been sanctioned, out of which 649 are \nfunctional. Opening of new J awahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (JNVs) is a continuous \nprocess which depends on the willingness of the concerned State Government/UT \nadministration to make available requisite suitable land free of cost for construction \nof the permanent building and making available require d temporary building, free of \nrent, to run the Vidyalaya till the permanent building is constructed. However, actual \nsanction and opening of new JNV depends on the availability of funds and approval \nby the Competent Authority.  \n \n02 JNVs have been set up at  Mungeshpur (North West District) and Jaffarpur \nKalan (South West District) in Delhi. 07 more JNVs had been sanctioned in \nNovember, 2016 for the districts of East Delhi, North East Delhi, West Delhi, North \nDelhi, South Delhi, South East Delhi and Shahdara. Schools will commence after \nGovernment of NCT of Delhi makes available the requisite e xtent of land and \ntemporary accommodation for these Vidyalayas.  \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |215", "t": "Cooperative Sugar Factories", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.215 \nANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n \nPROMOTION OF TOURISM IN RAJASTHAN AND GUJARAT \n \n215. SHRI NARANBHAI KACH