me of Incentivisation of Panchyats is released to the best performing Panchayats selected \nthrough a national competition for the National Panchayat Awards of various categories.    For \nthe State of Tamil Nadu, dues of Central Finance Commission Grants are not pending as the \naward period 2015 -20 of Fourteenth Finance Commission (XIV FC) is already over and the \n\nFifteenth Finance Commission (XV FC) Grants have been released upto the first installment \nof Basic (Untied) Grants for FY 2021-22. \n(d) Does not arise in view of (c) above.   \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to part (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.269 \nAnswered on 20.07.2021 regarding ‘Funds Released for Panchayati Raj’ \n \nState-wise release of funds under the Scheme Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan during \n2019-20 and 2020-21 \n \n \n \n \n \nSl. No. State/ UTs 2019-20 \n(Rs. in crore) \n2020-21 \n(Rs. in crore) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 0 22.339 \n2 Andaman  & Nicobar Islands 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 39.59 0 \n4 Assam 23.22 26.1159 \n5 Bihar 0 0 \n6 Chhattisgarh 0 4.0395 \n7 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 0 0 \n8 Daman & Diu 0 0 \n9 Goa 0 0 \n10 Gujarat 0 0 \n11 Haryana 0 9.89 \n12 Himachal Pradesh 10 22.098 \n13 Jammu & Kashmir 6.19 25.00 \n14 Jharkhand 0 2.34 \n15 Karnataka 0 0.439 \n16 Kerala 0 8.12955 \n17 Lakshadweep 0 0 \n18 Ladakh  2.1485 \n19 Madhya Pradesh 85.48 71.42 \n20 Maharashtra 8.44 66.76 \n21 Manipur 4.54 3.4127 \n22 Meghalaya 2.63 3.967 \n23 Mizoram 0.5 21.185 \n24 Nagaland 3.94 3.7217 \n25 Odisha 0 2.937 \n26 Punjab 0 13.45 \n27 Rajasthan 0 12.981 \n28 Sikkim 5.1 4.7475 \n29 Tamil Nadu 5.3 56.875 \n30 Telangana 0 12 \n31 Tripura 0 2.5304 \n32 Uttar Pradesh 169.92 32.54 \n33 Uttarakhand 23.79 26.751 \n34 West Bengal 44.10 33.52 \n Total 432.74 491.3378 \n\nState-wise release of funds under the Scheme of Incentivization of Panchayats during \n2019