1 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20TH JULY, 2021 \n \nWelfare Schemes For Fishermen Related to Covid Pandemic \n \n291.  PROF. SAUGATA RAY: \n  \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nमत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of the welfare schemes awarded for fishermen who suffered huge loss \ndue to the recent pandemic; \n \n(b)  whether the Government has any proposal to increase the quantity of Kerosene for \nfishermen; and  \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRYAND DAIRYING \n(DR. L. MURUGAN) \n(a): The Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying \nis implementing a flagship scheme namely “Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana \n(PMMSY) - to bring about Blue Revolution through sustainable and responsible development \nof fisheries sector in India” with an estimated investment of Rs. 20,050 crore for a period of 5 \nyears from financial year 2020 -21 to FY 2024 -25 in all States/Union Territories as a part of \nAatma Nirbhar Bharat Package  and welfare of fishers, fish farmers and fish workers at the \ncore of this scheme.   The welfare related activities supported u nder the PMMSY primarily \ninclude (i) insurance cover for fishers, fish farmers, fish workers , (ii) insurance for fishing \nvessels, (iii) livelihood support and nutritional support for socio -economically backward \nactive traditional fishers during fishing ban/lean period , (iv) supply of boats and n ets to \ntraditional fishermen, (v) supply of s afety kits for traditional and motorized fishing vessels , \n(vi) supply of communications and Potential Fishing Zones devices for traditional motorized \nboats, (vii) support for acquisition of technologically advanced fishing vessels for traditional \nfishermen, (viii)  Up-gradation of existing fishing vessels , (ix) Open sea cage culture, \nornamental fisheries, seaweed cultivation for creating alternative employment opportunities \n\nto coastal communities , (x) development of integrated modern fishing villages , (xi) \ndevelopment of fishing harbours, landing centres, cold chain facilities, transport vehicles, \nmarketing etc.  to facilitate the fishermen for smooth operation of fishing activities and \naugment financial returns.  \n \n(b) and (c) :   No, Sir. The Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry \nand Dairying has no such proposal.   \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |292", "t": "Campus of Tezpur University", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 292 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20TH JULY, 2021/ ASHADHA 29, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nADVANCED WEAPONRY WITH TERRORIST ELEMENTS \n \n†292.      SHRI RAHUL KASWAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that terrorists  have more advanced \nweapons and ammunition and resources available with them; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Government has prepared to  equip security forces \nwith advanced systems to counter the terrorists; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n(a) to (c): Terrorists have been using modern weapons and equipments to \ncommit terrorist acts across the world. Combat against terrorism is a \ncontinuous process. The Government has been strengthening its counter \nterrorism apparatus including equipping security forces and intelligence \nagencies with requisite resources, equipments, wea ponry, modern \ntechnology, training, etc.   \n****** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|STARRED   |293", "t": "Financial Assistance to Odisha", "head": "����������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������\n��\n��������������������\n����������������������������������������������������\n