ade for Financial Year 2020-2021; \n(b) the details of funds released for Panchayati Raj in the Financial Year 2019- 2020 and 2020-\n2021, State-wise; \n(c) whether there are dues pending in the allocation of funds to the State of  Tamil Nadu; and \n(d) if so, the reasons thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n \n(a)  A sum of Rs.690.00 crore (Revised Estimate) was provided to Ministry of Panchayati Raj \n(MoPR) for the year 2020-21, out of which Rs.546.94 crore was allocated for strengthening \nPanchayati Raj Institutions and incentivisation for their developmental works under the  \nCentrally Sponsored Scheme-Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA) and Incentivisation of \nPanchayats, a Central component of RGSA.  Under the Fifteenth Finance Commission Award, \nan amount of Rs.60750 crore was allocated to Panchayati Raj Institutions during 2020-21.   \n(b)    The State-wise release of funds under the schemes of Ministry of Panchayati Raj (MoPR) \nand out of awards of Fourteenth Finance Commission and Fifteenth Finance Commission are \ngiven at Annexure.   \n(c) No prior allocation of funds is made to any States under the Schemes of Ministry of \nPanchayati Raj. The funds under the RGSA Scheme is released based on the annual action plan \nsubmitted by the State concerned including the State of Tamil Nadu and funds under the \nscheme of Incentivisation of Panchyats is released to the best performing Panchayats selected \nthrough a national competition for the National Panchayat Awards of various categories.    For \nthe State of Tamil Nadu, dues of Central Finance Commission Grants are not pending as the \naward period 2015 -20 of Fourteenth Finance Commission (XIV FC) is already over and the \n\nFifteenth Finance Commission (XV FC) Grants have been released upto the first installment \nof Basic (Untied) Grants for FY 2021-22. \n(d) Does not arise in view of (c) above.   \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n