nawareness campaign ‘Crop Insurance Week/Fasal Bima \nSaptah’ was \ninitiated by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare between 1st July \n2021 to 7\nth\n \nJuly 2021 under Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav\n, \n \nan initiative to celebrate 75 years \nof India’s independence, in all the\n \ndistricts/areas notified under\n \nPradhan Mantri Fasal \nBima Yojana (PMFBY)/Restructured Weather Based Crop Insurance Scheme (RWBCIS) \nwith special emphasis on 75 aspirational/tribal districts\n.\n  \nThe State\n-\nwise details of \nselected 75 aspirational/tribal districts is \nannexed\n.\n \n  \nT\nhe\n \ncore focus o\nf the campaign was \nt\no increase\n \nthe \nawareness\n \nand benefits of the scheme\n,\n \nsensitize the stakeholders and to \nincrease overall\n \nenrollment of farmers, \nthereby helping them \nto \nreap the benefits\n \nof crop \ninsurance\n \nwith special focus on\n \nidentified aspirational/tribal d\nistricts\n. \n \nT\no \nincrease the \ncrop insurance penetration t\nhe campaign strategy aimed at: \n \n \ni\n.\n \nM\nobilization of multi\n-\nlevel stakeholders \nfor successful implementation of \nCrop \nInsurance Week \nviz\n \nStat\nes/UTs\n, \nB\nanks, \nCommon Service Centers (\nCSCs\n)\n, \nI\nnsurance \nC\nompanies\n(ICs)\n \nincluding\n \ngrassroot level association with \nAgricultural \nTechnology Management Agency (\nATMA\n)\n \nfunctionaries\n, Panchayati Raj Institutions \n\n(PRI), \nFamer Producer  Organizations (\nFPO\ns\n)\n,\n \nPrimary Agricultural Credit Society \n(\nPACS\n) etc.\n \nii\n.\n \nA \n360\n-\ndegree execution plan of all \nIn\nformation, Education and Communication \n(\nIEC\n)\n \nactivities at the grassroots level through channels such as awareness \nvehicles, TV shows, print media, digital media, \n \nOut of Home (\nOOH\n) advertising\n, \nbehavioral change communication (Nukkad Nataks), etc.\n \niii\n.\n \nA\n \nuniform communication, key messages, and branding across all kharif 2021 \nnotified locations\n.\n  \n \nThe campaign was launched by \nthe\n \nUnion Minister for \nAgriculture and Farmers \nwelfare \nalong with\n \nrelease\n \nof\n \nPMFBY e\n-\nBrochure, FAQ Booklet and a \nPMFBY/RWBICS Guide\nbook to assist farmers and ground level coordinators in \nunderstanding the basics of the scheme. \n \nDuring the entire duration of the campaign, farmers were engaged through multiple \nIEC activities with\n \nthe\n \nsupport of State Government and local level organizat\nions viz \nAgricultural Technology Management Agency (\nATMA\n)\n \nfunctionaries\n, Panchayati Raj \nInstitutions (PRI), \nFa\nr\nmer Producer  Organizations (\nFPOs\n)\n, Banks,\n \nPri\nmary \nAgricultural Credit Societies\n \n(\nPACS\n),\n \nCommon Service Centers (CSCs), \nI\nnsurance \nC\nompanies\n \n(ICs)\n.\n \nFollowing are the grassroot activities undertaken in the above\n-\nmentioned \nS\ntates to \ncreate widespread awareness\n \nand to increase crop insurance penetration\n \nduring \nthis week:\n \ni\n.\n \nA total of 24 IEC Vans travelled in all 75 blocks of 75 Districts during kharif \n2021 \ninforming farmers on benefit of crop insurance, enrolment process and other \nscheme related information.\n \nClose to 500 vans were additionally deployed by \nInsurance Companies at individual level in other districts.\n \nii\n.\n \nMore than 16 thousand ground level IEC \nactivities viz farmer meeting, village \nlevel sensitization activities were reported by various stakeholders. \n \niii\n.\n \nA total of \n5\n \ncrore audio \ncalls \nwere sent to farmers of all districts including \naspirational and tribal districts. \n \niv\n.\n \nDistribution of PMFBY print \nmat\nerial \nsuch as pamphlets, flyers across entire \ndistricts and blocks\n.\n \nv\n.\n \nSpecial engagement workshop/seminars with Women Farmers\n \nvi\n.\n \nBanners and Wall Paintings \n \nvii\n.\n \nNukkad Natak done in various villages/ blocks\n \nviii\n.\n \nDisplay of Hoardings/Posters in Hindi and other regional l\nanguages \n \nix\n.\n \nAwareness and engagement activities on MyGov portal \nintroducing \nPMFBY \nQuiz and Crop Insurance Pledge\n.\n \n \nThe Crop Insurance week saw media coverage in close to 230 editions of national \nand regional newspapers and their e\n-\nversions, with state published Print "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |286", "t": "Access to CCTNS", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 286 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20TH JULY, 2021/ ASHADHA 29,1943 (SAKA) \n \nACCESS TO CCTNS \n \n286.  DR. SHASHI THAROOR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has decided to allow  private companies to \nhave access to the Crime and  Criminals Tracking Network Systems \n(CCTNS) and other  Government databases for conducting background  \nchecks; \n \n(b) if so, whether all companies has been allowed to access the CCTNS; \n \n(c) whether the Government will allow this access to  those companies \nwho pay for this information; \n \n(d) if so, the details of the payment required and the  criteria used to \ndetermine the same; and \n \n(e) the safeguards that will be put in place to protect  the data of citizens \nand prevent its misuse in the hands  of private entities by the \nGovernment? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI AJAY KUMAR MISHRA) \n \n(a) No, Sir. \n(b) to (e) Does not arise in view of reply to part (a). \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |287", "t": "Scholarships under SHREYAS", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *287 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.08.2021 \n  \nPMKVY IN TAMIL NADU \n \n*287.   DR. T.R. PAARIVENDHAR:  \n  \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n  \n(a)  the total number of youths, male and female se parately, who have been enrolled \nfrom Tamil Nadu for skill development training unde r the Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas \nYojana (PMKVY) during the last three years; \n \n(b)  the number of youths in the State, male and fe male separately, who have got \nemployment or placement after the training during the last three years; \n \n(c)  the total amount allotted and spent for this p rogramme during the last three years; \n \n(d) whether the Union Government proposes to set up  Skill Development Training \nCentres in the backward district of Perambalur in Tamil Nadu; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reas ons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER  \n  \nMINISTER OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) to (E) of LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *287 TO BE ANSWERED ON 09.08.2 021 ASKED BY DR. \nT.R. PAARIVENDHAR REGARDING ‘PMKVY IN TAMIL NADU’ \n \n(a) Under the Skill India Mission, Ministry of Skil l Development and Entrepreneurship \n(MSDE) is implementing its flagship scheme, Pradhan  Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana \n(PMKVY). Under PMKVY, in the last three years (2018 -21), 1.83 lakh female candidates \nand 1.88 lakh male candidates have been enrolled in the State of Tamil Nadu. \n \n  \n(b)       PMKVY has two training components, namely , Short-Term Training (STT) and \nRecognition of Prior Learning (RPL). STT is linked to placement, while RPL does not \nmandate placements as it recognizes the existing skills of candidates. Under STT-PMKVY, \nin the last three years (2018-21),  1.22 lakh (0.94  lakh female and 0.28 male) candidates \nhave been, as on 10.07.2021, certified in the State  of Tamil Nadu; out of which 0.82 lakh \n(0.63 lakh female and 0.19 male) candidates have been placed.  \n  \n(c)        Under PMKVY, during the last three years  (2018-21), the total budgetary allocation \nwas Rs. 5,230.05 crore; out of which, Rs. 5,037.19 crore was disbursed to implementing \nagencies, i.e., the National Skill Development Corp oration (NSDC) for Central component, \nand State Skill Development Mission (SSDM) / State Governments for the State \ncomponent for the implementation of the PMKVY acros s the country including the State of \nTamil Nadu.  \n  \n               Out of total disbursed funds in last  three years (2018-21) under PMKVY, Rs. \n172.43 crore (Rs. 138 crore under Central Component  and Rs. 34.43 crore under State \nComponent) was disbursed for the implementation of the scheme in the State of Tamil \nNadu.  \n  \n(d)       Ministry promotes establishment of model and aspirational skill centre known as \nPradhan Mantri Kaushal Kendra (PMKK) for imparting skill training in every district of the \ncountry, including  the district of Perambalur in t he State of Tamil Nadu. Ministry through \nNSDC provides funding support upto 75% of the proje ct investment for establishment of a \nPMKK in a district.  \n  \n               Also, under STT-PMKVY, training cent res (TCs) are empanelled for imparting \nshort duration training across the country, includi ng the district of Perambalur in the State \nof Tamil Nadu. Under RPL-PMKVY, candidates are oriented in camps, employer premises, \nPMKKs and large/medium enterprises.  \n  \n(e)               Till now, in the State of Tamil N adu, 35 PMKKs have been established, \nincluding 1 PMKK in the district of Perambalur. Als o, under STT-PMKVY, 2,325 TCs have \nbeen empanelled in the State of Tamil Nadu, includi ng 27 TCs in the district of \nPerambalur.  \n  \n******  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |288", "t": "Schemes under Disha Committee", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 288 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nSCHEMES UNDER DISHA COMMITTEE \n \n288.  SHRI SUNIL BABURAO MENDHE: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(