y to be \ncompleted?  \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n\n(a)  The existing criteria for declaration of State roads including \nState Highways (SHs)  as new National Highways ( NHs) include \nroads running through length / breadth of the country, connecting \nadjacent countries, National Capitals with State Capitals / mutually \nthe State Capitals, major ports, non -major ports, large industrial \ncenters or tourist centers, roads meeting ver y important strategic \nrequirement in hilly and isolated area, arterial roads which enable \nsizeable reduction in travel distance and achieve substantial \neconomic growth thereby, roads which help opening up large tracts \nof backward area and hilly regions (ot her than strategically \nimportant ones), achieving a National Highways grid of 100 km, etc. \n(b) State /UT-wise details of State roads, including SHs, declared \nas NHs during the last three years, including such roads in the State \nof Gujarat and North-eastern States, are annexed. \n(c) to (e) The Ministry keeps on receiving proposals from various \nState Governments/UTs, etc., including the proposals from the State \nGovernment of Rajasthan, for declaration  / upgradation  of State \nroads including SHs as new NHs. The Ministry considers declaration \nof some State roads including SHs as NHs from time to time based \non the requirement of connectivity, inter -se priority and availability \nof funds. \n  \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART  (b) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 505 ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 ASKED \nBY SHRI BALAK NATH, SHRI JASWANT SINGH BHABHOR, SHRI \nSUMEDHANAND SARASWATI  AND SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY  \nREGARDING UPGRADATION OF NHS \nState /UT -wise details of State roads, including SHs, declared as \nNHs during the last three years:- \nSr. No. Name of State/UT NH No. Length (In Km) \n1 Andhra Pradesh \n516C, 167BG, 544F, 130CD, 365BG, 167K, 342, \nNE7, 440,516B, 340B,