, State/year-wise; and \n \n(c) Whether the Government has launched any scheme for elimination \nof Single Use Plastic, air pollution and soil pollu tion and if so, the \ndetails thereof ?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a) : The State-wise break-up of Open Defecation Fr ee (ODF), ODF+ and \nODF++ certified cities is at Annexure-I. \n \n(b) : The state-wise break-up of total toilets cons tructed and under-\nconstruction in urban areas as on 31.06.2021 under Swachh Bharat \nMission is at Annexure-II. Year-wise data, however, is not maintained. \n \n(c) : Government has launched National Clean Air Pr ogramme (NCAP) \nas a long-term, time-bound, national level strategy  to tackle air \npollution across the country in a comprehensive manner with targets \n \n…2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \n \nto achieve 20% to 30% reduction in PM 10 and PM 2.5 level by 2024.  \n \nThe Plastic Waste Management Rules, 2016, prohibits  manufacture, \nimport, stocking, distribution, sale and use of car ry bags and plastic \nsheets less than fifty microns in thickness in the country.  \n \nThe Solid Waste Management Rules 2016, notified by Ministry of \nEnvironment & Climate Change (MoEF&CC), inter-alia , addresses the \nissues relating to soil pollution in the country. \n \nFinance Minister in her budget speech has announced  implementation \nof Swachh Bharat Mission 2.0, with a total financia l allocation of \n\u00011,41,678 Crore, over a period of five years from 20 21-2026, \naddressing, inter alia , issues relating to single use plastic, air and so il \npollution. \n  \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Part (a) of Lok Sa bha Unstarred Qn No. 506 due for \nanswer on 22.7.2021 regarding State-wise break-up o f ODF, ODF+ and ODF++ certified \ncities.  \n \n \nSl. \nNo  \nState/  \nUnion Territory \nNo. of Urban Local \nBodies (ULBs) \ncertified ODF  \nNo. of ULBs \n