oney subsidy of 25% of the project cost in rural areas\n \nand 15% in urban areas\n. The \ndistrict wise applications received under the scheme and the  district wise list of  units set up and \nmargin money released under PMEGP in the state of Odisha are given at Annexure\n-\nI and \nAnnexure\n-\n \nII.  \n \n \nMinistry of MSME also i\nmplements Credit Guarantee Scheme for Micro and Small \nEnterprises which is mandated to facilitate credit guarantee support for collateral free / third\n-\nparty \nguarantee\n-\nfree loans to the Micro and Small enterprises (MSEs), especially in the absence of \ncollat\neral. It facilitates access to finance for un\n-\nserved and under\n-\nserved segments of society and \ngeographies.  Under this scheme, guarantee is extended by Credit Guarante\ne\n \nTrust for Micro and \nSmall Enterprises (CGTMSE) to the proposals brought to it by the Ba\nnks/Member Lending \nInstitutions and no eligible proposal is denied.  District wise list of beneficiaries of the Credit \nGuarantee Scheme in the State of Odisha is at Annexure\n-\nIII. \n \n \n \n****\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure I r\neferred to in the  Lok Sabha Un\nstarred  Question No. 507 due for answer on \n22.07.2021\n \n \nDistrict wise no. of application received under PMEGP in Odis\nh\na during last Five Years.\n \nSr.No\n \nDistrict Name\n \nNo. of Application received \n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n1)\n \nAngul\n \n468\n \n337\n \n277\n \n223\n \n310\n \n2)\n \nBalangir\n \n724\n \n663\n \n512\n \n520\n \n415\n \n3)\n \nBaleswar\n \n936\n \n902\n \n1246\n \n806\n \n979\n \n4)\n \nBargarh\n \n990\n \n396\n \n269\n \n232\n \n349\n \n5)\n \nBhadrak\n \n1161\n \n941\n \n774\n \n527\n \n746\n \n6)\n \nBoudh\n \n315\n \n215\n \n196\n \n171\n \n168\n \n7)\n \nCuttack\n \n1526\n \n1280\n \n1165\n \n902\n \n1359\n \n8)\n \nDeogarh\n \n160\n \n166\n \n183\n \n242\n \n159\n \n9)\n \nDhenkanal\n \n688\n \n4