ATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PORTS, SHIPPING AND WATERWAYS\n(SHRISHRIPAD NAIK)\n(a) Yes Sir. Ministry of Port, Shipping & waterways has received a representation on\nsetting up of empty container yard and servicing centre at Morbi, Gujarat.\n(b), (c) & (d) The matter has been considered in consultation with Logistic Division,\nMinistry of commerce, who has communicated that they have not been mandated for\nlaying down criteria for setting up of empty container yard and service center. However,\nthey have opined that such facilities will lead to optimal use of stock and overall\nreduction in logistics cost."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |562", "t": "Rural Areas Covered under Jal Jeevan Mission", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 562  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021  \n  \nRURAL AREAS COVERED UNDER JAL JEEVAN MISSION \n562. ADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state: \n(a) the details of rural population covered under Jal Jeevan Mission so far, State-wise;  \n(b) whether the Government has set any target for a chieving the goals under Jal Jeevan \nMission;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the progress achieved by each State; and  \n(d) the details of the funds released to the States  including Kerala and the amount utilized so \nfar? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL ) \n \n (a) to (c) Since August, 2019,Government of India,  in partnership with States, is \nimplementing Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) – Har Ghar Ja l, to provide tap water connection to \nevery rural household by 2024, with an estimated outlay of Rs. 3.60 lakh Crore. \n \nAt the time of announcement of Jal Jeevan Mission o n 15th August, 2019, out of 18.93 Crore \nrural households, 3.23 Crore households (17%) were reported to have tap water connections. \nAs on date, out of 18.98 Crore rural households acr oss the country, 7.76 Crore households \n(40.89%) are reported to have potable tap water sup ply in their homes. The State/ UT-wise \ndetails of rural households having tap water supply is at Annex–I. \n \n(d)  The details of the funds released and the amou nt utilized (including unspent balance of \nprevious years) under JJM during 2019-20, 2020-21 & 2021-22 is at Annex–II. \n*****  \n  \n\nAnnex – I \nAnnex referred in the statement of reply to Lok Sabha  Unstarred  Question No. 562 due \nfor reply on 22.07.2021  \n \nState/ UT-wise status of tap water connections in rural households (HHs) \n(as on 19.07.2021) \n(Number in lakhs) \nS. \nNo.  \nState/ UT Total rural \nHHs as on \n15.08.2019  \nRural HHs with \ntap water \nconnection as on \n15.8.2019  \nTotal \nrural \nHHs as \non date \nRural HHs given \ntap water \nconnections since \n15.8.2019  \nRural HHs with \ntap water supply \nas on 19.7.2021 \nNo. %age No. %age No. %age \n1. A & N Islands 0.65  0.29  43.85  0.62  0.33  53.98  0.62  100  \n2.  Andhra Pradesh  95.66  30.74  32.14  95.17  17.02  17.89  47.77  50.19  \n3.  Arunachal Pradesh  2.18  0.23  10.47  2.18  0.86  39.63  1.09  50.1  \n4.  Assam  63.35  1.11  1.76  63.35  7.83  12.36  8.95  14.12  \n5.  Bihar  1,83.54  3.16  1.72  1,72.21  143.52  83.34  1,46.68  85.18  \n6.  Chhattisgarh  45.48  3.2  7.03  45.48  2.59  5.70  5.79  12.73  \n7.  DNH and D&D  0.60  NR  NR  0.85  0.84  99.14  0.84  99.14  \n8.  Goa  2.63  1.99  75.7  2.63  0.64  24.30  2.63  100  \n9.  Gujarat  93.03  65.16  70.05  92.92  13.19  14.20  78.35  84.32  \n10.  Haryana  28.94  17.66  61.03  30.99  12.12  39.10  29.78  96.1  \n11.  Himachal Pradesh  17.04  7.63  44.75  17.04  5.95  34.90  13.57  79.67  \n12.  J&K  18.17  5.75  31.66  18.35  4.43  24.15  10.19  55.51  \n13.  Jharkhand  54.09  3.45  6.38  59.23  4.51  7.61  7.96  13.44  \n14.  Karnataka  89.61  24.51  27.35  91.19  5.92  6.49  30.43  33.37  \n15.  Kerala  67.15  16.64  24.78  70.69  6.93  9.80  23.57  33.34  \n16.  Ladakh  0.44  0.