vy management in \nRs.2500 Crore Karvy Scam in which several lakh customers have not yet received their money \nalong with the time by which SEBI plans to take these actions; \n(c) the  actions  which  SEBI  plans  to  take  against NSE management and broker in Rs.1000 \nCrore BMA Wealth case along with the time by which SEBI plans to take  these  actions;  and \n(d) the  actions  which  SEBI  plans  to  take  against NSE management and Anugrah stock \nbroker owners in Rs.1200 crore scam?  \n \nANSWER \nSHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FINANCE \n \n(a) CBI has registered a case in the matter of preferential access at the co-location facility \nof National Stock Exchange of India Limited, vide RC No.AC I 2018A0011 dated 28.05.2018, \nunder section 120B & 204 of Indian Penal Code, Sections 7, 12 & 13 (2) read with 13(1)  (d) \nof Prevention of Corruption Act, 1988 and under section 66 of Information Technology Act, \n2000. Presently, the case is under investigation. \n \n(b) SEBI has already passed orders in the matter of Karvy Stock Broking Limited (KSBL) \nand initiated action against Directors and Key Management Personnel (KMP) of KSBL . In \naddition, adjudication proceedings have been initiated against both NSE and Bombay Stock \n\nExchange (BSE) for violating provisions of SEBI circulars. This is in addition to the criminal \ncomplaints filed by the NSE and its declaration of the broker as a defaulter. Claims of investors \nhave been invited through a public notice.  \n(c) SEBI has already passed orders in the matter of BRH Wealth Kreators Limited (BRH; \nformerly BMA Wealth Creators Limited) and against HDFC Bank Limited in the matter. \nFurther, SEBI has initiated enforcement proceedings against BRH, BRH Commodities Private \nLimited (BRHCPL), their KMPs and related entities as well as approved filing prosecution \nagainst BRH, BRHCPL and their KMPs for mis -utilisation of funds and securities of clients, \ndiversion of funds and non-cooperation. This is in addition to the criminal complaints filed by \nNSE and its declaration of the broker as a defaulter.  Claims of investors have been invited \nthrough a public notice.  \n(d) SEBI has already passed order in the matter of Anugrah Stock & Broking Private \nLimited (ASBPL) and initiated enforcement proceedings against ASBPL, its related entities \nand their KMPs. Application for prosecution has been filed against aforesaid en tities, for \nengaging in Derivative Advisory Services in the nature of Portfolio Management Services \npromising assured returns without seeking registration under relevant SEBI Regulations. This \nis in addition to the criminal complaints filed by NSE and its declaration of the broker as a \ndefaulter. Claims of investors have been invited through a public notice.  \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |590", "t": "Solar Pumps to Farmers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-590 \nANSWERED ON-22/07/2021 \n \nSOLAR PUMPS TO FARMERS \n \n590. SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any scheme to provide solar pumps to farmers in the \ncountry, if so, the details and salient features thereof; \n(b) the number of solar pumps installed under various schemes in this regard, State/UT-\nwise including Bihar; \n(c) the details of the amount received by farmers who have installed these solar pumps, \nState-wise; \n(d) the distribution of the amount of surplus electricity that has been sold by farmers to \nDISCOMs under these schemes, State/UT-wise; and \n(e) the details of the ‘dark zones’ identified under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Suraksha \nevam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM-KUSUM); and \n(f) the criteria used to determine them along with the number of solar pumps installed \nin these ‘dark zones’ for revenue earned by farmers in these zones? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) to (c) The Ministry of New and Renewable energy (MN RE) launched Pradhan Mantri \nKisan Urja Suraksha evam Utthaan Mahabhiyan (PM -KUSUM) on 8.3.2019, with the \nfollowing three components: \n(i) Component-A: installation of 10,000 MW aggregated capacity small solar power plants \neach of capacity up to 2 MW on the barren/fallow land of the farmers; \n(ii) Component-B: installation of 20 lakh standalone off-grid solar water pumps; and \n(iii) Component-C: solarization of 15 lakh existing grid-connected agriculture pumps. \n \nUnder the Scheme 30.8 GW solar power capacity will be created by 2022 with central \nfinancial support of Rs. 34,035 Crore.  \n \nUnder the Component-B and Component-C of the Scheme, the Central Government provide s \nas subsidy 30% of benchmark cost or cost discov ered through tender, whichever is lower. In \naddition to central financial support at least 30% of cost of solar pump is provided by the \nrespective State Government. In case of North-Eastern states including Sikkim; hilly states of \nHimachal and Uttarakhand;  UTs of Jammu and Kashmir, Ladakh, Andaman & Nikobar \nisland and Lakshadwwep, higher central financial support of 50% of benchmark cost or cost \ndiscovered through tender, whichever is lower is being provided.  \n \n\nA total of 47146 nos. of solar pumps have been  installed under Component -B; and 580 nos. \nof existing pumps have been solarized under Component -C. State -wise details of the \nstandalone solar pumps installed/ pumps solarized under PM -KUSUM Scheme and funds \nreleased is placed at Annexure-I. \n \n(d) Provision of sale of surplus power through solarisation of individual grid –connected \npumps has been made  under Component -C of PM -KUSUM Scheme. As solarisation of \npumps has recently started on ground, billing of surplus power sold by farmers is yet to be \nreported by the state implementing agencies.  \n \n(e)&(f) Dark zones or over -exploited ground water resources are identified by Central \nGround Water Board (CGWB) in association with the State ground water organisations.  \n \nThe ground water resources are assessed in units  i.e blocks/ talukas/ mandals/ watersheds. \nThese assessment units are categorized for ground water development based on two criteria - \na) stage of ground water development, and b) long -term pre and post monsoon water levels. \nCGWB has notified 162 Over -exploited areas in the country for regulation of ground water \ndevelopment and management.  \n \nState Implementation Agencies for PM-KUSUM Scheme so far have not reported installation \nof solar pumps in the ‘Dark Zones’.  \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nAnnexure-I referred in reply to Part (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Question No. 590 to be answered \non 22.07.2021 on ‘Solar Pumps to Farmers’ \nDetails of solar pumps installed/ pumps solarized and funds released under PM-KUSUM \nScheme \n \nS. No. States No. of Pumps \nInstalled/ existing \npumps solarized  \nas on 30.06.2021 \nCentral Financial \nSupport released  \n(Rs. Crore) \n1.  Gujarat 379 3.95 \n2.  Haryana 14254 62.70 \n3.  Himachal Pradesh 121 2.79 \n4.  Jharkhand 1467 16.05 \n5.  Karnataka 96 1.26 \n6.  Madhya Pradesh 7234 71.07 \n7.  Manipur 2 0.36 \n8.  Odisha 203 0.77 \n9.  Punjab 2925 20.05 \n10.  Rajasthan* 15549 94.03 \n11.  Tamilnadu 1016 11.21 \n12.  Tripura 215 3.96 \n13.  Uttar Pradesh 4265 20.37 \n  Total 47726 308.57 \n \n*including 580 nos. of existing  grid connected agriculture pumps solarized in the State of \nRajasthan \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |591", "t": "Urban Sports Infrastructure Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †591 \nANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 \n \nUrban Sports Infrastructure Scheme \n \n†591. SHRIMATI RANJEETA KOLI: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the names of the projects sanctioned during the  last three years under \nUrban Sports Infrastructure Scheme; \n \n(b) the number of projects out of them completed safer; and \n \n(c) the names of the projects not being completed within their scheduled \ntime out of the above mentioned sanctioned projects? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR } \n \n(a) The Urban Sports Infrastructure Scheme (USIS) was operational from  \n2010-11 to 2015 -16, wherein a total of sixty-two sports infrastructure \nprojects got sanctioned. \n \n(b) Out of the sixty-two projects sanctioned under USIS, forty-one have been \ncompleted and ten foreclosed/cancelled. \n \n(c) The list containing  names of eleven projects which have not been \ncompleted within  the stipulated time and are still under progress is at \nAnnexure. \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART ( c) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTIO N NO. †591 ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 REGARDING \n“URBAN SPORTS INFRASTRUCTURE SCHEME ” ASKED BY SHRIMATI \nRANJEETA KOLI, HON’BLE MEMBER OF LOK SABHA \n \nS. \nNo. \nName of State / \nUnion Territory \nName of the project \n1.  Assam Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall SAI SAG \nCentre, S.S. Stadium, Tinsukia. \n2.  Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall at Gauhati \nUniversity, Guwahati. \n3.  Himachal \nPradesh \nLaying of Synthetic Athletic Track at Luhnoo \nGround, Bilaspur. \n4.  Kerala Construction of Multipurpose  Indoor Hall at \nPathanamthitta. \n5.  Nagaland Construction of Multipurpose Indoor at Dimapur. \n6.  Laying of Synthetic Football Turf at Jalukie, Pe ren \nDistrict. \n7.  Odisha Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall  at \nRavenshaw University, Cuttack, Odisha. \n8.  Rajasthan Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall at Karauli. \n9.  Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall at Alwar. \n10.  Tamil Nadu Laying of Six Lane  Synthetic Athletic Track in \nUdhagamandalam. \n11.  Jammu & \nKashmir \n(Now UT of \nLadakh) \nConstruction of a Multipurpose Indoor Hall at Leh. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |593", "t": "Tap Water to All", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 593 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 \n \nTAP WATER TO ALL \n \n593.   SHRI VINAYAK  RAUT: \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) aims to pr ovide tap water to all the households of \nour country by 2024 and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has recently reviewed th e performance of JJM in the country \nincluding Maharashtra; and \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH  PATEL) \n \n(a)  To make provision for potable tap water supply  to every rural home by 2024, \nGovernment of India is implementing Jal Jeevan Miss ion (JJM) in partnership with States, \nwith an estimated outlay of Rs. 3.60 lakh Crore. At  the time of launch of Jal Jeevan Mission \non 15 th  August, 2019, out of total 18.94 Crore rural house holds in the country, 3.23 (17%) \ncrore rural households had tap water connections. S ince then, 4.52 Crore (23.84%) rural \nhouseholds have been provided with tap water connec tions thus, as on date, 7.76 Crore \n(40.89%) rural households have provision of tap water supply. \n \n(b) & (c)  This Department is regularly reviewing t he implementation of Jal Jeevan Mission \nwith respective State governments to expedite the i mplementation of the mission to achieve \nthe goal in a time-bound manner. Annual Action Plan  (2021-22) of Maharashtra was \ndiscussed on 25 th  June, 2021, inter alia which included review of pr ogress made so far, and \nplanning and implementation of Jal Jeevan Mission t o make provision of tap water supply to \nevery home by 2024.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |594", "t": "Maintenance of Ambulances at Toll Plazas", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 594 \nANSWERED ON 22ND JULY, 2021 \n  \nMAINTENANCE OF AMBULANCES AT TOLL PLAZAS \n  \n594. SHRIMATI GEETA KORA: \n       SHRI JUGAL KISHORE SHARMA:  \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n  \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether it is a fact that the condition of ambulances deployed at \nmany toll-plazas in the country is pathetic and if so, the details thereof \nalong with the reaction of the Government thereto; \n  \n(b) the details of the complaints received regarding deployment of \ndysfunctional/unequipped ambulances and the action taken thereon by \nthe Government; and \n  \n(c) the number of road -accidents victims benefitted from the ‘Golden \nHour‘ Scheme during the last three years, State-wise? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \n  (SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n \n(a) Due to   non-uniformity of standards for ambulances, there was \nsome difference in the   types of ambulances deployed in different \nprojects. At some places, ambulances deployed are simple patient \ntransport vehicles only. Recognizing this, directions hav e been issued \n\nto field units to upgrade the existing ambulances to the standards of \nBasic Life Support (BLS)  ambulances as per AIS -125. Further, NHAI \nhas recently signed contract agreements for   supply, operation and \nmaintenance of 126 AIS -125 compliant Ba sic Life Support   \nambulances across the country. \n(b)  Road users   generally register all their highway related complaints \nthrough 1033 helpline   number and the same are duly addressed by \nthe corresponding Regional Offices and Project Implementation Unit s \nat local level itself. \n(c)   Such data is not maintained at Ministry level. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |595", "t": "Encroachment of Water Bodies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †595\nANSWERED ON 22.07.2021\nENCROACHMENT OF WATER BODIES\n†595. DR. KRISHNA PAL SINGH YADAV\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the number of water bodies in many States has decreased due to encroachement, unplanned\nurbanisation, industrialisation, lack of propoer management and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) whet her the Government has conducted any separate study on the condition, increase/decrease in\nnumbers of water bodies and status of their encroachment;\n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;\n(d) whether a Central database is being maintained on water bodies presentaly and if so, the details thereof;\n(e) whether it regularly compiles data on total number of water bodies, increase/decrease in their numbers\ndried up/extinct water bodies changes in land use of catchment areas on water bodies and encroachment etc;\nand\n(f) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI\n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT)\n(a) to (f) It is for the State Governments concerned to undertake enumeration, protection and management\nof water bodies in their respective States. However, this Ministry undertakes census of minor irrigation\nschemes from time to time, which also captures information pertaining to certain specific water bodies in\nthe country. As per the latest census, being 5 th census of minor irrigation schemes with reference year 2013 -\n14, there are 5,16,303 water bodies in the rural areas of the country, which are being used for minor\nirrigation. Out of these, 53,396 water bodies are not in use for various reasons such as non -availability of\nwater, siltation, salinity, etc. The commensurate figures as per 4 th Minor Irrigation Census undertaken by\nthis Ministry with reference year 2006 -07, are 5,23,816 water bodies in the rural areas being used for minor\nirrigation, out of which 80,128 water bodies not being in use.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |596", "t": "Funds under JJM", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 596 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 \nFUNDS UNDER JJM \n596.    SHRI  RAMDAS  C. TADAS: \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI  be pleased to state: \n(a)  the amount of funds allocated to the State of Maharashtra under Jal Jeevan Mission \n(JJM) including the names of works for which the am ount has been allocated along with the \ntime by which the work is likely to be completed; \n(b)  the total number of villages of the said State  including the number of houses targeted to \nget safe drinking water under the mission along with the time limit for the same; \n(c)  the dates on which the tender for the said wor ks have been invited; and \n(d)  whether  the said work has been started and if  so, the details of the works completed and \nif not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE  FOR  JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI  PRAHLAD  SINGH  PATEL) \n \n(a)& (d) In 2021-22 under Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM),  Rs. 7,064.41 Crore Central grant has \nbeen allocated to Maharashtra. As reported by the S tate Government, out of total 2,255 \nproposed water supply schemes worth Rs. 2,412.28 Cr ore, work order has been issued for \n2,043 schemes and 339 schemes have been completed. \n(b)   Out of total 40,596 villages having 142.36 la kh households in Maharashtra, as on date in \n9,018 villages, every household  is  reported to have provision of tap water supply. Remaining \n50.39 lakhs rural households in 31,578 villages are  planned to be provided with tap water \nconnection by 2024. \n(c) Under Jal Jeevan Mission, powers to plan, appro ve and implement schemes are vested \nwith State Government and therefore details of date s of tenders to be issued by the State \nGovernment is not maintained by this Department. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |597", "t": "Jal Shakti Abhiyan in Bihar and Gujarat", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †597\nANSWERED ON 22.07.2021\nJAL SHAKTI ABHIYAN IN BIHAR AND GUJARAT\n†597. SHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM\nSHRIMATI RAMA DEVI\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Jal Shakti Abhiyan has been implemented in Bihar and Gujarat;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) the details of the targets set under the said Abhiyan in Bih ar and Gujarat at present including the\npresent status of the works done thereunder?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI AND TRIBAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRI BISHWESWAR TUDU)\n(a) to (b) Ministry of Jal Shakti has taken up a nationwide campaign “ Jal Shakti Abhiyan - Catch the\nRain” (JSA:CTR) with the theme “Catch the rain, where it falls, when it falls” for creating appropriate\nrainwater harvesting structures in urban and rural areas of all the districts in the country including Bihar\nand Gujarat, with peopl e's active participation, during the pre -monsoon and monsoon periods. The\ncampaign, primarily focusing on saving and conserving rainwater, was launched by Hon'ble Prime\nMinister on 22 March, 2021, the world water day.\nCreation of new and maintenance of o ld Rainwater harvesting structures; revival of traditional\nrainwater harvesting structures like stepwells etc; enumeration, geo -tagging, making inventory of water\nbodies, reuse and recharge of bore wells; watershed development and intensive afforestation p reparation\nof scientific water conservation plans and setting up of Jal Shakti Kendras are part of the campaign.\n(c) The details of progress made under the Jal Shakti Abhiyan: Catch the Rain campaign upto 12.07.2021\nas uploaded on JSA:CTR Portal (jsactr:mowr.gov.in) by the Central stakeholder Ministries/Departments in\nrespect of their Key Performance indicators is annexed.  State Governments have also been request to\nupload the information regarding works undertaken by them with state and local funds under JSA:CTR\ncampaign.\n*****\n\nANNEXURE\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†597 TO\nBE ANSWERED IN LOK S ABHA ON 22 .07.2021 REGARDING “ JAL SHAKTI ABHIYAN I N\nBIHAR AND GUJARAT”.\nSTATE\nDetails of progress made\nWater\nConservation\nand\nRainwater\nHarvesting\nRenovation\nof\nTraditional\nWater\nBodies\nReuse and\nRecharge\nStructures\nWatershed\ndevelopment\nIntensive\nAfforestation\nAwareness\nGeneration\nBihar 13570 2013 13717 7877 1836 1336\nGujarat 1531 1691 359 5677 2567 25687\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |598", "t": "Special Body to Implement NRLP", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †598\nANSWERED ON 22.07.2021\nSPECIAL BODY TO IMPLEMENT NRLP\n†598. SHRI TAPIR GAO\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government is planning to set up any special body to implement National River Linking\nProject (NRLP);\n(b) if so, the details along with the present status thereof;\n(c) whether the Gov ernment has received any suggestion from the States with regard to the said project;\nand\n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the action taken by the Government in this regard?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI\n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT)\n(a) & (b)  The Ministry of Jal Shakti considering setting up of a National Interlinking of Rivers Authority\n(NIRA) for implementation of the Interlinking of Rivers (ILR} projects. The proposal is under\nexamination.\n(c) & (d)  The Government is pursuing the ILR program in a consultative manner. All the Pre -feasibility\nReports / Feasibility Reports / Detailed Project Reports of the ILR projects are circulated to\nconcerned/party States for their views/suggestion and they are suitably addressed to the extent possible in\nthe respective reports.\nAll the comments/issues received from the States are deliberated in the Special Committee for\nInterlinking of Rivers, constituted in September, 2014, in its various meetings.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |599", "t": "Solar Plants", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-599 \nANSWERED ON-22/07/2021 \n \nSOLAR PLANTS \n+599. SHRI DEEPAK BAIJ \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state:  \n(a) the quantum of electricity in megawatt currently being generated by the solar plants in the \ncountry and the targetted production thereof by the year 2024; \n(b) the name of the places in Chhattisgarh where solar energy plants are likely to be set up; and \n(c) the places at which new solar plants are likely to be set up during the next three years under \nthe Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) in the country? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a): As on 30.6.2021, solar power projects of 42,335.45 MW capacity have been installed for \nproduction of electricity from solar energy in the country. The Government has set a target of \nachieving 100 GW of installed solar power capacity by December, 2022. \n(b): The Government of Chhattisgarh has reported that 26 solar plants of 649.21 MWp have been \nplanned. The details are given at Annexure. \n(c): Government have allowed 100% Foreign Direct Investment under the automatic route in \nRenewable Energy (RE) projects including solar energy projects. As such, any developer can \nset up RE projects using foreign investment. \n***** \n  \n\n \nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 599 FOR 22.07.2021 \nLIST OF GROUND MOUNTED GRID CONNECTED SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC \nPOWER PLANTS UNDER INSTALLATION IN CHHATTISGARH \n \n  (As On 10-07-2021) \nSN Project Location MWp \n1 Village- Singhanpur, District- Mahasamund 40 \n2 Village- Singhanpur, District- Mahasamund 25 \n3 Village-Agar, Tehsil-Dhamdha, District- Durg 3.5 \n4 Village- Lalpur, Block- Navagarh, District-Bemetara (C.G.) 12.5 \n5 Village- Lalpur, Block- Navagarh, District-Bemetara (C.G.) 37.5 \n6 Village-Chandi/Khaparadih, Post Office- Grasim Vihar, Tehsil-\nSimga, District-Balodabazar (C.G.) 18.9 \n7 Village-Chouranga&Darchura, Tehsil-Simga, District-\nBalodabazar (C.G.) 70 \n8 Village- Chandanu, Tehsil- Bemetara, District-Bemetara (C.G.) 1.2 \n9 Village- Chandanu, Tehsil- Bemetara, District-Bemetara (C.G.) 12 \n10 Village-Kakrel, Nawagaon&Baigatola, District-Rajnandgaon \n(C.G.) 70 \n11 Village-Batauli, District-Sarguja, Chhattisgarh 50 \n12 Village-Kansabel, District-Jashpur, Chhattisgarh 50 \n13 Village-Dhuma, District-Rajnandgaon, Chhattisgarh 5 \n14 Village-Thenghabhat, Ahiwara, Tehsil-Dhamdha, District-Durg 2 \n15 Village-Neonara, Tehsil-Berla, District-Bemetara 1.321 \n16 Village-Bahera, Tehsil-Berla, District- Bemetara 11 \n17 Village-BijaBhata, Tehsil-Dongargaon, District- Rajnandgaon 8 \n18 Village-Indawani, Tedesara, District-Rajnandgaon (C.G.) 5 \n19 Village-Sarada, Tehsil-Berla, District-Bemetara (C.G.) 3 \n20 Village-Bagdumar, Ahiwara, District-Durg (C.G.) 1 \n21 Village-Badghoom, Tehsil-Dongargaon, District-Rajnandgaon \n(C.G.) 12 \n22 Village-Badghoom, Tehsil-Dongargaon, District-Rajnandgaon \n(C.G.) 12 \n23 Village- Salhebhata, Gram Panchayat-Tendukona, Tehsil-\nBaghbahara, District-Mahasamund (C.G.) 2 \n24 Village- Padumtara/Basula/ Khairjhiti, District-Rajnandgaon \n(C.G.) 25 \n25 Village-Patan, Tehsil-Bhatapara, District-Bhatapara-Baloda \nBazar (C.G.) 12 \n26 \nVillage-Dhaba, Rengakathera, Dundera, Amlidih, Kohka, \nOdarbandh, Tolagaon, Margaon, Girgaon, Ghughwa, District- \nRajnandgaon (C.G.) \n160 \nTOTAL 649.921 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |6", "t": "Promotion of Digital Banking", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO-*6 \nANSWERED ON- 19.072021 \n \nWage Revision in LIC \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the proposal regarding wage revision of officers and staff working in the \nLife Insurance Corporation of India is pending with the Government since the year \n2017; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the time by which the Government is likely to \nconsider the said proposal; and  \n(c) the reason for delay in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE FINANCE MINISTER \n(SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n(a) to (c):  No, Sir. Wages of officers and other employees of the Life Insurance \nCorporation of India have been revised with effect from 1.8.2017. \n** \n \n \n  *6. SHRI SATYADEV PACHAURI:  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |60", "t": "New Schools and Colleges in Uttar Pradesh", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION AND LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 60 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19th July, 2021 \n \nNew Schools and Colleges in Uttar Pradesh \n \n†60. SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT: \n   \nWill the Minister of Education be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of new high school and new inter  colleges required in Uttar Pradesh State as \nper the norms of Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan; and \n(b)  whether the Government has taken any steps to  establish high school and inter colleges in \nUttar Pradesh as per the norms of Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION  \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n  \n(a) & (b) : The Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan \n(RMSA) was under implementation since 2009 to 2017 -18 for universalizing secondary \neducation in the country.  \n  \nThe RMSA along-with  Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and Teacher Education (TE ) have \nbeen subsumed in an Integrated Centrally Sponsored Scheme for School Education  - Samagra \nShiksha from 2018-19. It is an overarching programme for the school education sector extending \nfrom pre-school to class XII and aims to ensure inclusive and equ itable quality education at all \nlevels of school education.  \n The Annual Work Plan & Budget (AWP&B) under Samagra Shiksha is prepared by the \nStates and UTs based on the norms of the scheme, requirements and priorities of State under \ndifferent interventions including the requirement of the new High Schools and Senior Secondary \nSchools. These plans are then appraised and approved/estimated in consultation with the States \n\nand UTs as per the programmatic and financial norms of the scheme and availability of \nbudgetary resources.  \nUnder erstwhile RMSA till 2017-18 and Samagra Shiksha effective from 2018-19, 1551 \nSecondary schools and 6 Senior Secondary schools have been sanctioned to the State of Uttar \nPradesh out of which 1483 secondary schools have become functional. \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |600", "t": "Schemes for Khadi Promotion", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 600\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021\n \n \nSchemes for Khadi Promotion\n \n \n600.\n \n \nDR. RAM SHANKAR KATHERIA:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND\n \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate:\n \n(a) \n \nwhether the steps are being taken by the Government to encourage the use of \nKhadi; \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) \n \nthe steps taken by the Government to incentivise Khadi workers during the last \nthre\ne years?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NARAYAN RANE)\n \n \n \n(a)&(b):\n \nNumber of steps/initiatives have been taken by the Ministry of MSME, \nthrough Khadi & Village Industries Commission (KVIC), to encourage the use of \nKhadi\n.  Details are at \nAnnexure\n.\n \n \n(c):\n \nTo incentivise Khadi workers, direct 30% financial assistance is provided to the \nKhadi Artisans under Modified Market Development Assistance (MMDA) scheme \nsince 2016\n-\n17. \n \n \nThe incentive provided to Khadi artisans during th\ne last three years are as \nfollows:\n \n \nYear\n \nAmount of Incentive to Khadi \nArtisans\n \n(Rs. in crore)\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n82.25\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n93.57\n \n2020\n-\n21 (Provisional)\n \n70.08\n \n \n \n* * *\n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n \n \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a)&(b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred\n \nQuestion No. \n600 for answer on 22.07.2021\n \n \nThe steps/initiatives taken by the M/o MSME to encourage the use of Khadi is as follows:\n \n \n1.\n \nTo ensure genuineness of Khadi “Khadi Mark” has been notified by Government of \nIndia. \n \n2.\n \nMinistry of Commerce and Industry, \nGovt. of India has extended KVIC, the status of \nDeemed Export Promotion Council (EPC), for supporting promotion of Khadi and \nVillage Industries products in international market. 2816 Khadi Institutions have taken \nits membership to enter the field of export\n. KVIC through its assisted institutions and \nunits participates in various international exhibitions.\n \n3.\n \nTie up arrangements with premier institutions like Federation of Indian Export \nOrganization (FIEO), World Trade Centre (WTC), Indian Trade Promotion \nOrgan\nization (ITPO), Trade Promotion Council of India etc., for invigorating business \nopportunities in the overseas market by conducting exhibitions and workshops for \nKhadi Institutions.\n \n4.\n \nTie up arrangements for bringing out innovative export quality product des\nigns with \nNIFT, etc.\n \n5.\n \nTo create unique identity of “Khadi”, a separate HS code for 22 items of Khadi product \nis also requested from the Ministry of Commerce for recognizing the potential of export \nof Khadi & Village Industries (KVI) products.  \n \n6.\n \nKVIC has eng\naged fashion designer of national and international repute for Fashion \nDesigning to make Khadi products more competitive and appealing in the domestic as \nwell as overseas market segment.\n \n7.\n \nKVIC participated/exhibited/promoted Khadi\n \nproducts in various exhibitions during \ndifferent occasions which gives an opportunity and a strong platform to showcase \nquality of KVI products.\n \n8.\n \nConsidering the need of present generation and the effect of COVID\n-\n19 pandemic, \nKVIC has started online sellin\ng of all KVI products. KVI products are available to \nevery Indian’s door step through \nwww.ekhadiindia.com\n, \nwww.khadiindia.gov.in\n.\n \n9.\n \nMoU has been \nsigned\n \nwith the Ministry of\n \nTribal Affairs, Govt. of India for supply of \nKhadi Polyvastra fabric for making uniforms for its 75,000 students worth Rs. 14.77 \ncrore.\n \n10.\n \nMoU has been signed with the Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) canteens under \nclarion call of our \nHon’ble\n \nPrime Minis\nter for “Atmanirbhar Bharat” for supply of KVI \nproducts.\n \n11.\n \nMarketing tie\n-\nups with Railways, Department of Posts, Air India, ONGC and other \nGovt. organizations.\n \n12.\n \nTie\n-\nups with Corporates namely Raymond, Aditya Birla and Arvind\n \nMills to enhance \nvisibility and sales of Khadi products\n \n13.\n \nLaunched ‘franchise scheme’ to expand the sales distribution network.\n \n14.\n \nKVIC has taken up production of Khadi Mask as an income generation activity for the \nCOVID\n-\n19 pandemic hit artisans of Khadi Insti\ntutions. So far supply of more than 25 \nlakhs Khadi masks worth Rs 6.51 crore made by Khadi Bhavan, New Delhi.\n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |603", "t": "Roads under CRIF", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 603 \nANSWERED ON 22ND JULY, 2021 \n  \nROADS UNDER CRIF \n \n603.SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \n \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken or proposes to take any steps to \nconstruct roads in backward areas/ villages of Mishrikh Parliamentary \nConstituency in Uttar Pradesh under the Central Roads and \nInfrastructure Fund (CRIF);  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) to (c) Ministry vide OM No. RW/NH -15017/46/2018-P&M dated \n31st January 2020 has issued guidelines/criteria for allocation of funds for \ndevelopment of state roads under the Central Roads and Infrastructure \nFund (CRIF) Act 2000. As per these guidelines, the state government/UTs \nshall identify and priorities the project s for release of Funds as per the \ndefined criteria and furnish necessary details of the projects to the \nCentral Government. Ministry has not yet received any proposal from \nstate government to construct roads in backward area/villages of Mishrikh \nParliamentary Constituency in Uttar Pradesh.     \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |606", "t": "Impact of Covid on MSME Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 606\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON\n \n22.07.2021\n \n \nImpact of Covid on MSME Sector\n \n \n606.     SHRI DR. PRITAM GOPINATHRAO MUNDE:\n \n \nSHRI GIRISH BHALCHANDRA BAPAT:\n \n \nSHRI \nRAHUL RAMESH SHEWALE:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n(a) \n \nwhether Covid\n-\n19 pandemic had a very severe adverse impact on the entire MSME \nsector in the country;\n \n(b)  \n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n(c)  \n \nwhether t\nhe Covid\n-\n19 pandemic placed MSME owners, employers, workers and      \ninstitutions associated with the MSME sector into a very difficult state where no one had \nany experience to handle this kind of situation;\n \n(d)  \n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n(e) \n \nthe\n \nextent to which the Covid\n-\n19 pandemic adversely impacted MSMEs‘ earnings;  \nand\n \n(f)  \n \nthe steps taken or proposed by the Government to revive the MSME sector?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NARAYAN RANE)\n \n \n(a) \nto (f)\n:\n   \nThe adverse impact of Covid\n-\n19 pandemic has been felt on the economy\n \nincluding on the MSME sector. To revive the MSME sector, the \n \nGovernment has taken \nthe following steps:\n \n \n \ni.\n \nRs. 20,000 crore Subordinate  Debt for MSMEs.\n \nii.\n \nRs.3 lakh crores Collateral free\n \nAutomatic Loans for business, including \nMSMEs.\n \niii.\n \nRs. 50,000 crore equity infusion through MSME Self\n-\nReliant India Fund \n \niv.\n \nNew Revised criteria of classification of MSMEs.\n \nv.\n \nNew Registration of MSMEs through ‘Udyam \nRegistration’ for Ease of Doing \nBusiness.\n \nvi.\n \nNo gl\nobal tenders for procurement up to Rs. 200 crores.\n \n \n \n \nAn Online Portal “Champions” has been launched on 01.06.2020 by Hon’ble Prime \nMinister. This covers many aspects of e\n-\ngovernance including redressal of grievances and \nhandholding of MSMEs. \n \n \n \nRBI has \nalso announced several measures to Reduce Financial Stress of MSMEs.\n \n \n*****\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|6|UNSTARRED |607", "t": "NH Projects in Punjab", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 607 \nANSWERED ON 22nd JULY, 2021 \n  \nNH PROJECTS IN PUNJAB \n607. SHRI GURJEET SINGH AUJLA: \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the details and present status of National Highways (NHs) which \nare under construction in the State of Punjab; \n(b) whether all these NHs are likely to be completed within their \nstipulated time period and if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the funds allocated and released